{"id": "swebq0149", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.27, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1706, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Abstract art;German Expressionism;Expressionism;Der Blaue Reiter", "query": "what kind of painter was wassily kandinsky?", "transcript": "What kind of painter was Wassily Kandinsky?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Wassily Kandinsky was a Russian painter and art theorist. He is known as one of the pioneers of abstract art. Kandinsky believed that colors and shapes could express emotions directly, without the need for realistic representation. He often combined bold colors and geometric forms to create dynamic compositions that conveyed deep spiritual and emotional experiences. His work helped lay the foundation for modern abstract painting.", "answer_ms": 1743}
